# PHINEAS AND FERB SONG OF THE DAY WEBSITE

## Welcome to PNFSOTD.com
I made this as a joke but I ended up trying to do it somewhat optimally as an exercise.

## How does it work?
0. I seed my database with all P&F songs from Spotify using seed/seed.py.
    - Structure your `seed/.env` like this:
```
CLIENT_ID=xxx
CLIENT_SECRET=xxx
```
    - And you'll need to go to the Spotify developer portal for that info.
1. When you visit the website, it calls the function `getSongOfTheDay(utc_offset)`.
2. First that checks `cache.json` to see if the song of the day has already been determined.
3. If not, it pops a track off of `tracklist.json` and looks up the info with the Spotify API.
5. Once the track of the day has been determined, it is written to the cache and it expires in a few days (UTC).
6. If the track is the last one on the tracklist, I also call `populateTracklist()`.

## Other things
1. As I mentioned I wanted to keep web-fetching to a minimum, hence the cache and tracklist. I also made the fetching parallel per album, so it is really fast. I got rate limited when I tried to do it per track, and not worth the hassle since it only runs one time ever. Fun to learn about Python threads.

2. There are probably edge case bugs, I tried my best to test every possible combo of cache, tracklist, and .env. The thing that is hard to test is realtime checking. Will have to monitor as the days pass to make sure the song changes.

3. I think this is funny, please check it out and listen to Phineas and Ferb music (if you don't have Spotify use Google.)
`https://pnfsotd.com/`